WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:00.913
- [Kelly] You have a

00:00:00.913 --> 00:00:01.890
new 16 month old, right?

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.814
A little baby?
- I do.

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:03.745
(Audience cheers)

00:00:03.745 --> 00:00:04.593
- [Kelly] That's exciting,

00:00:04.593 --> 00:00:07.280
What's one of your toughest
mom moments that you've had?

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.590
- Well, recently, very recently,

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.470
he's 16 months now and, you know,

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.440
it's like you learn what they understand

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.273
and what they don't,

00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:17.340
what they're absorbing,
what they're not absorbing.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.570
And he was eating dinner,

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.710
and my husband said something
that really annoyed me

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.031
as husbands do.

00:00:22.031 --> 00:00:22.864
(audience laughs)

00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:23.763
- I don't know what you're referring to.

00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:24.596
(audience laughs)

00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:25.540
- Yeah, and I like

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.990
kinda raised my voice at him,

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.170
I was probably like, "Ryan,
blah blah blah blah!"

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.897
And Baz, my son, he went:

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:33.147
"Momma,

00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:35.090
no, no, no."

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:35.923
(audience giggles and coos)

00:00:35.923 --> 00:00:36.756
- Oh!
- Like that.

00:00:36.756 --> 00:00:38.100
And I was like

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:38.950
Like I,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.557
like, my heart broke, 'cause I was like

00:00:40.557 --> 00:00:41.967
"Oh! No!" I like--

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:42.880
- "'cause I'm a horrible human."

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.830
- No, well, yeah!

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.880
It was just like he was
putting me in my place,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.090
I was kind of really proud
of him for doing that.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.187
But, you know, it was like

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:50.500
"You're right. I'm sorry.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.430
Mommy shouldn't raise her voice at daddy."

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:53.920
and I had to apologize to him.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.259
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, my poor children.

00:00:55.259 --> 00:00:56.218
(Kelly chuckles)

00:00:56.218 --> 00:00:57.251
(audience laughs)

00:00:57.251 --> 00:00:59.050
You know, usually we don't argue really,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.510
my husband and I, but like

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.630
we're both very passionate.
- Yes, very passionate.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:03.920
- You're household is probably what,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.806
you know, what you should do.

00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:06.639
(both laugh)

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:07.588
And mine is like,

00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:09.031
waaah!

00:01:09.031 --> 00:01:11.020
- I am also very pa--

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.270
like, people call it screaming,

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.400
I just call it talking.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.467
- Exactly!
- This is how I talk.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.306
- That's what I say.
- I'm allowed to talk.

00:01:15.306 --> 00:01:16.447
- I am too.

